# VIGIL SaaS money-IN drain, STRIPE lane — config for vigil-billing-drain-stripe.service   (MONEY path)
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/billing-drain-stripe.env with mode 0600 (`install -m 600 …`). PREFER injecting the secrets
# below from your secret manager (GO-LIVE §9b); this file is the documented FALLBACK. NEVER commit it.
# Every value below is the owner's, set at deploy. Leave them empty here. Only the drain process receives this
# file's values: the unit's heartbeat hook runs with an allow-listed env.
# ONE DRAINER: use the vigil-billing-drain-stripe TIMER or a manual `sigil billing-drain watch --provider stripe` — never both.
# =====================================================================
# Paths in THIS file must be ABSOLUTE (systemd does NOT expand %h inside an EnvironmentFile value).

# REQUIRED to run at all (the Stripe lane is DEFAULT-OFF and refuses unless this is exactly 1). Also set it in
# ~/.config/vigil/alerts.env so `vigil alerts` watches this unit fail-closed from the start.
# VIGIL_STRIPE_BILLING_DRAIN_ENABLED=1

# REQUIRED: the Stripe adapter opt-in (it refuses to construct without it).
# VIGIL_BILLING_ENABLE_STRIPE=1

# REQUIRED: the Stripe endpoint's signing secret (the SAME value the proxy's /webhooks/stripe route uses). It must
# differ from the Flutterwave VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# VIGIL_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# REQUIRED: a RESTRICTED Stripe API key (read Checkout Sessions, Invoices, Subscriptions; write Checkout Sessions)
# for the MANDATORY server-side re-fetch. Its live/test prefix must match the endpoint's mode.
# VIGIL_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# REQUIRED: the Stripe API version this integration was tested against (sent as Stripe-Version on every call).
# VIGIL_STRIPE_API_VERSION=

# REQUIRED, ALWAYS — even if you never moved it: the cockpit's SIGIL_HOME, as an absolute path (GO-LIVE §2; outside
# ~/.sigil, also add it to the unit's ReadWritePaths). The drain mints onto the spine under it and never falls back
# to ~/.sigil: without this line it REFUSES (the unit goes FAILED). It also refuses when ~/.sigil/cockpit.env names a
# different SIGIL_HOME, or when this directory holds no owner identity. Never moved: SIGIL_HOME=/home/USER/.sigil
# SIGIL_HOME=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil

# The Stripe spool whose incoming/ is drained (default %h/.sigil/stripe-billing-spool). It MUST equal the proxy's
# VIGIL_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SPOOL and must NOT be the Flutterwave billing spool. REQUIRED once SIGIL_HOME is moved: the
# drain refuses the ~/.sigil default while SIGIL_HOME is elsewhere (unless VIGIL_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SPOOL below confirms
# it).
# VIGIL_STRIPE_BILLING_SPOOL=/home/USER/.sigil/stripe-billing-spool

# OPTIONAL: a copy of the proxy's VIGIL_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SPOOL (the drain cannot see the proxy's env). When set, the
# drain refuses (the unit goes FAILED) a spool that is not this directory.
# VIGIL_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SPOOL=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil/stripe-billing-spool

# OPTIONAL (NET-2b, default OFF): park a webhook whose Stripe re-fetch hit a TRANSIENT failure (timeout, reset, HTTP
# 408/425/429/5xx) for a bounded retry instead of quarantining it on sight. A 404 or any other refusal quarantines.
# VIGIL_NET_RECOVERY_ENABLED=1
